# Azuarif: Unofficial AZ-900 Practice Tool

> Know why, not just what.

**Unofficial learning project. Not affiliated with or endorsed by Microsoft. All questions are original and based on the public AZ-900 skills outline on Microsoft Learn.**

Built for the Vibe Coding Hackathon: AZ-900 Exam Prep Edition (#1MillionDevs, Power Learn Project Africa).

## The problem
Many learners practise with questions but never understand why an answer is right or wrong.

## The solution
Azuarif is a quiz app that gives instant feedback, a clear explanation for the right answer, a reason why each wrong option is wrong, and an "Explain with an African example" button for beginners. Results are shown by AZ-900 topic.

## Features
- Original questions organised by topic
- Instant correct/wrong feedback with explanations
- Reasons why the other options are wrong
- African real-life examples (matatus, SACCOs, apartment rentals)
- Score by topic with a simple readiness message
- Mobile-friendly design

## Live demo
https://mwangi-builds.github.io/Azuarif-AZ-900-quiz/

## Tech stack
HTML, CSS, JavaScript. Optional: Supabase Edge Function + Claude for live example generation. Built with AI assistance from Claude.

## How to run
1. Clone this repo.
2. Open `index.html` in a browser.

## Project structure
- `index.html`: page structure
- `css/style.css`: styling
- `js/app.js`: quiz logic and scoring
- `js/explain.js`: African example feature
- `data/questions.js`: question bank
- `feature/docs/promt.md`: prompts used

